@@ -68,3 +69,21 @@ provide instant updates, with reconnect recovery and a lightweight HTTP fallback
 The configured single Puma process shares the local Action Cable adapter; no
 external service or background worker is required. See [live-game design notes](docs/live-games.md)
 for presence semantics, state invariants, privacy, and deployment details.
+
+## Scores and prizes
+
+In quiz **Settings**, set **Number of winners** (minimum 1, default 3).
+Each correct final answer scores one point. Ties use the sum of elapsed times
+of correct answers, from the shared question opening to the player's last pick.
+Scores stay hidden on phones until **End quiz**.
+
+At the end, the big screen lists all players in order, and each phone shows
+**Place X of Y** and its points. **Top N** selects the highest-ranked eligible
+players. **Draw** keeps players above the cutoff's points and randomly fills
+the remaining prizes from the entire points tie, ignoring speed. Each click
+redraws. Zero-point players never win; if too few players have points, all
+those with points win. **Reset winners** clears the selection.
+
+**Winner** marks and **You won!** announcements update live and survive reloads.
+See [scoring and prizes notes](docs/scoring-and-prizes.md) for implementation
+details, legacy data handling, and tests.
